          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Doctrinal Adjunction
            is the title of a 1974 paper (
            %a{:href => "#Kelly"}> Kelly
            ) that gives conditions under which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjoint morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \dashv u
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"} counit
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi l
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_l
            for some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monad"} 2-monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %p
            Here
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi l
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_l
            is the 2-category of strict
            = succeed "-algebras," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+morphism"} lax T-morphisms
            = succeed "-transformations," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            The term ‘doctrinal’ refers to the concept
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/doctrine"} doctrine
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "doctrine#as_2monads"} 2-monad
          %h2#statement Statement
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \dashv u
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              in some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monad"} 2-monad
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              between
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar u
              making
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (u,\bar u)
              a lax
              = succeed "-morphism" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f
              making
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,\tilde f)
              a colax
              = succeed "-morphism;" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mates"} mates
              with respect to the adjunctions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi T
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T f \dashv T u
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \dashv u
          %p
            The proof (
            %a{:href => "#Kelly"}> Kelly
            ) relies solely on the properties of the mate correspondence.
          #strength.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For the unit and counit of the adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \dashv u
              to be
              = succeed "-transformations," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Alg
                        %mi l
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_l
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f
              have an inverse
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f
              that makes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,\bar f)
              into a lax
              = succeed "-morphism," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,\bar f)
              into a strong
              = succeed "-morphism." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            Again, the proof hinges on the properties of mates: we take the conditions for the unit and counit to be
            = succeed "-transformations" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi f
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi T
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T f \dashv T u
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \dashv 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f
            is the mate of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar u
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f
            are mutually inverse.
          %p It follows that
          #mate.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f, \bar f) \dashv (u, \bar u)
              in
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi l
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_l
              if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \dashv u
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f
              has inverse
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f
              \= the mate of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar u
          %p Dually, one has:
          #dual.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f, \bar f)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (u, \bar u)
              be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colax+morphisms"} colax morphisms
              of
              = succeed "-algebras." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \dashv u
              as functors.
            %ol
              %li
                There is a bijection between lax structures on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                and colax structures on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              %li
                The adjunction
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \dashv u
                lifts to an adjunction
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi u
                      %mo ,
                      %mover
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f, \bar f) \dashv (u, \bar u)
                if and only if the lax structure
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde u
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
                induced by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,\bar f)
                is inverse to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar u
                (meaning, in particulat, that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi u
                      %mo ,
                      %mover
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (u,\bar u)
                is strong).
          %h2#in_terms_of_double_categories In terms of double categories
          %p
            Doctrinal adjunction can be stated cleanly in terms of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+categories"} double categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            there is a double category
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %strong Alg
            whose objects are
            = succeed "-algebras," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-morphisms," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-morphisms," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            that make a certain cube commute; see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+category+of+algebras"} double category of algebras
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi l
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_l
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_c
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Alg
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Sq
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \mathbf{Alg} \to \mathbf{Sq}(K)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Sq
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Sq}(K)
            is the double category of squares or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quintets"} quintets
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %p
            It is straightforward to verify that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjunction"} conjunction
            in the double category
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %strong Alg
            is precisely an adjunction in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            between
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %strong Alg
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/companion"} companion
            precisely when it is a
            %em strong
            (= pseudo)
            = succeed "-morphism." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                The forgetful double functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi T
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Alg
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Sq
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon T \mathbf{Alg} \to \mathbf{Sq}(K)
                creates conjunctions. I.e. given a horizontal arrow
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Alg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \mathbf{Alg}
                and a left conjoint
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(u)
                (i.e. a left adjoint of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
                in
                = succeed ")," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Alg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\mathbf{Alg}
                lying over
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A\to B
                be a vertical arrow in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Alg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \mathbf{Alg}
                (i.e. a colax
                = succeed "-morphism)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'\colon A\to B
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u\colon B\to A
                be horizontal arrows (i.e. lax
                = succeed "-morphisms)." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %ol
                %li
                  Data making
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
                  a horizontal companion of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                %li
                  Data making
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
                  a right conjoint of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                %li
                  Data making
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
                  a left adjoint of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
                  in the horizontal 2-category.
          %p
            Of these, the second is actually a general statement about companions and conjoints in any double category. Of course, the first is a special property of the forgetful double functor from the double category of
            = succeed "-algebras." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#monoidal_categories Monoidal categories
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            the 2-monad whose 2-algebras are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a lax
                = succeed "-morphism" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
            %li
              %p
                an oplax
                = succeed "-morphism" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oplax+monoidal+functor"} oplax monoidal functor
          %p The above theorem then asserts
          .un_corollary
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              For two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R)
              between monoidal categories,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is oplax monoidal precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is lax monoidal.
          %p Moreover:
          .un_corollary
            %h6#corollary_2 Corollary
            %p
              For two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functors"} lax monoidal functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \dashv R
              between monoidal categories to be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+adjunction"} monoidally adjoint
              it is necessary and sufficient that:
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \dashv R
                as functors
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                is strong monoidal, and the inverse of the lax monoidal structure on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mate"} mate
                of the lax monoidal structure of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oplax+monoidal+functor"} oplax monoidal functor
            and at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+adjunction"} monoidal adjunction
            for more details.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+adjunction"} monoidal adjunction
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Kelly
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Kelly"}> Max Kelly
              ,
              %em Doctrinal Adjunction
              Lecture Notes in Mathematics, (1974), Volume 420/1974, doi:
              %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.1007/BFb0063105"} 10.1007/BFb0063105
          %p The following article explains the double category perspective:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Comparing composites of left and right derived functors
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0706.2868"} arXiv:0706.2868
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://nyjm.albany.edu/j/2011/17-5.html"} journal abstract page
          %p Doctrinal adjunction is related to monadicity in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Lack"}> Stephen Lack
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Morita contexts as lax functors
